.TH FACTORTEST 1
.SH NAME
factortest \- regression test for factor(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B factortest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Factortest
loads
.BR /p9/dis/factor.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR runstring(args) ,
and checks a representative set of numbers against golden output: 1
(no factors), a small prime, a composite with repeated small factors,
a larger prime that exercises the trial-division wheel out to its own
square-root bound, a perfect number, and multiple arguments factored
in one call.
.PP
.IR Factor (1)
is a translation of Plan 9's own
.B sys/src/cmd/factor.c
rather than a workalike, so every expected value here was checked
independently (a from-scratch trial-division factorization, not
derived from this file's own wheel logic), then cross-checked
separately during development against both GNU coreutils'
.I factor
and the real Plan 9
.I factor
binary (this tree's local
.B plan9port
checkout) - all three agree on every case here.
.PP
Prints one line per failure to standard error, a final
.IR N " passed, " N " failed"
summary to standard output, and exits with a non-nil status if
anything failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/factortest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR factor (1)
.SH BUGS
Runs
.I factor
in-process via its
.B runstring
seam, not as a spawned subprocess reading real standard input - so it
does not exercise
.IR factor 's
own
.B init ,
or its zero-argument (read numbers from standard input until a
non-positive sentinel) form, at all.
